
######## Wednesday, the 29th of April, 1931 (mild (4° to 13°C)) ########
   ◆ Ada's past: "He was always good to her, and she was fond of him."
   ◆ Arthur's past: He had always been accustomed to live within his income, and had saved a little.
   ◆ Mr. Thomas's past: He has never speculated.
   📅 Ada means to: Thursday: does her washing, and cleans the kitchen | Friday: goes out and buys food, and pays rent, and looks for work | Saturday: mends Bert's clothes, and sort the linen
   📅 Arthur means to: Thursday: sorts his papers in a drawer, and begin to bind a volume of insurance reports
   📅 Mr. Thomas means to: Thursday: visits his married sister in the country | Friday: makes up his books | Saturday: pays the charwoman
   ⚠ Mr. Thomas knows what has not happened yet (us_president_elected): Franklin Roosevelt.
