   Arthur [a quarter past six in the morning at Hales' house in Islington] (as usual)
      → Read the Daily Herald over breakfast (1d.)
      ⇒ Arthur read the Daily Herald: CAIRO. Forty-one persons were counted dead today, with scores injured, because a hot box set a train afire. As the Cairo-Alexandria Express rolled along yesterday afternoon, laden with a holiday crowd of pleasure seekers, a hot box developed on one of the third class coaches and set the coach afire. The train’s motion pulled… LONDON. Police of much of the world today made preparations to suppress disorders during widespread observance tomorrow of International Labor Day. In England, May Day celebrations have gone somewhat out of fashion and little beyond soap box oratory and a few small processions was expected in London, but elsewhere in Europe… IN PARLIAMENT. The House of Commons yesterday was occupied with the Amendment Of Law, and with the Channel Islands (Repre-Sentation) Measure, 1931.
